# Lane M6 rig A/B — the subagent surfaces (picker + farewell)

The accelerated protocol (lane/accel): iterate `--quick` (1 run,
80x24 — the sidebar script keeps its 160x36 override) with the
ref-capture cache ON; the cache only replays cross-run-CONFIRMED
steps (the stability warmer ran `--measure-stability 5 --filter
subagent` first: 0/4 scripts fully cacheable — spinner/blink/exit
classes flip run-to-run — so every verdict below is effectively
LIVE on the ref side; the `ref` column shows `cache(part)` because
the handful of confirmed steps inside each script do replay).

## The stale-binary trap (found the hard way)

The rig's `build_binary` reuses ANY existing `target/debug/
opencode-rust` — three A/B rounds ran a pre-fix binary while the
source had moved (the mismatch set looked "unfixable"). Counter-
measure baked into this lane's loop: `rm -f target/debug/
opencode-rust` before EVERY rig invocation. This is the same
"rig 陈旧二进制坑" the lane/C merge battles recorded (ROADMAP).

## A/B record (our side: OC_SUBAGENT_OPENTUI, ref: live bun)

| script          | size   | flag=0 mismatch union                                | flag=1 mismatch union                                | verdict |
| --------------- | ------ | ---------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------- |
| subagent-basic  | 80x24  | 8 or 11 steps (run 1/2)                              | 11 steps (runs 1+2)                                  | identical modulo the (b)-coin |
| subagent-browser| 80x24  | 15 steps                                             | 15 steps                                             | IDENTICAL |
| subagent-sidebar| 160x36 | 16 steps                                             | 16 steps                                             | IDENTICAL |

The basic/browser/sidebar mismatch unions decompose EXCLUSIVELY
into the documented backlog classes — verified against the per-step
dumps (`/tmp/opencode/tui-diff/<tag>/sNN.{ref,our}.txt`):

* `(b)-class per-run values` — the reply stats row
  (`Build · Fake Model · Nms · X.X tok/s`), the thought duration
  (`+ Thought · Nms`), and the exit step's session-id characters
  (`opencode -s ses_…`, text-only) — flip within the SAME flag
  run-to-run;
* `(b)-class home-placeholder coin` — `boot`/`dismiss`/
  `variant-dismiss` on subagent-basic: absent in flag=0 run 1,
  present in flag=0 run 2 AND both flag=1 runs (the coin proof
  pair at the end of the lane ran 0/1 back-to-back: BOTH produced
  the identical 11-step union);
* the pre-existing `models-*` dialog backlog (mm2 class, both
  paths, documented since lane/diff-rt);
* the ref-side LIVE sidebar context meter (subagent-sidebar, the
  `SidebarSections.context` seam — pre-existing on both paths).

The PICKER/CARD/CHILD/FAREWELL cells themselves are byte-identical
with the ref on both paths: after this lane's geometry fixes the
per-step mismatch counts on the picker steps dropped to exactly the
stats-row cell deltas (e.g. picker-open: 57 cells, ALL inside
`row 10: Build · Fake Model · …`), and child-view's remaining
deltas live inside the `+ Thought · Nms` row.

## Lane geometry fixes this A/B drove (the =0 fallback path too)

1. `picker mount budget`: the panel's height BUDGET must be
   PANEL_ROWS (11), not PICKER_MOUNT_ROWS (12) — the mount's 12th
   row is the pad BELOW the panel; the ref's transcript viewport
   runs one row longer than the prompt mount's arithmetic
   (session.rs).
2. `user-block rail`: the user message's rail keys on the SESSION's
   agent (`local.agent.color(session.agent)`, index.tsx:2200) —
   `TranscriptOptions::user_rail` + `Store::session_agent_rail_color`
   (the child view's `general` hue; fixtures keep the first hue).
3. `up-at-top closes even on an empty list` (subagents-tab.tsx:
   145-151 precedes the move guard) — `picker_move`'s `down` guard
   stays.

